Carafe: with CompactReturns, a return keeps only the call-return stack check in line (pop, compare, branch on a miss,
ret). The lookup for a return that misses the stack, with the profiler's miss count, goes after the block's code with
the other out-of-line pieces. With the bridge return in place almost no return misses, so those 40-64 bytes at every
return site sat in hot instruction cache lines unused; on the A57 an instruction costs three to four times as much
once the hot code outgrows the 48 KB instruction cache. Off by default.
MIT, as the files it changes.

